 4. 🚨 Senate shocker: Toss-up Kansas 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Chart: The New York Times In a major Senate shift, Cook Political Report yesterday moved Kansas — yes, Kansas — from lean Republican to toss-up, citing "perhaps a perfect confluence of events."

 Cook also moved New Hampshire from toss-up to lean Democrat, and North Carolina from lean Democrat to likely Democrat. 📊 The N.Y. Times/Siena poll (charted above) gives Democrats a lead among likely voters in the Senate races in Texas and Alaska, each of which usually votes Republican.

 Democrats have an edge in Ohio, which has trended red for years. Republicans have an edge in Iowa. Kansas, which hasn't voted for a Democratic senator since 1932, is neck and neck. More from the poll (gift link). 

 
 
