 5. 📺 Fox News turns 30 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Nielsen. Chart: Christine Wang/Axios Fox News turns 30 today with a distinction few legacy TV networks can claim: Its ratings lead over rivals has never been wider, Axios Media Trends author Sara Fischer writes. 

 Last year, the network averaged 1.69 million total-day viewers, compared with 551,000 for MS NOW and 432,000 for CNN. Through Sept. 29, Fox is outpacing CNN and MS NOW combined this year in both total day viewership and primetime. Then and now: Sean Hannity, who joined the network in 1996, hosts the primetime "Hannity." Photos: Fox News The big picture: Fox News launched Oct. 7, 1996. Fox News Media president and executive editor Jay Wallace , who has been with the network alongside CEO Suzanne Scott since launch, attributes the brand's durability to consistent ownership and strategy.

 "We've had a pretty consistent model for 30 years," Wallace told Sara. He credited the Murdochs' stewardship for allowing the network to be creative in developing new products and pursuing challenging stories. Keep reading ... Watch the first broadcast ... Anchor reflections ... Anniversary page . 

 
 
