 7. 🎤 Alex Taylor: Treat adoptions like a child&#x27;s birth 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Alex Taylor accepts the Angels in Adoption award. Photo: Congressional Coalition on Adoption Institute

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Alex Taylor — chairman and CEO of Cox Enterprises , which owns Axios — said in accepting an award from the Congressional Coalition on Adoption Institute ( CCAI ) that employers can take a very tangible step to encourage employees to give vulnerable kids a new home and a new start.

 "One thing we do that many other companies don't," he said, "is we treat adoptions the same way we treat the birth of a child. Families that adopt a child are given the same benefits in terms of parental leave and financial assistance as birth parents." 🏛️ The big picture: The Congressional Coalition on Adoption ( CCA ) is Congress' historically largest bicameral, bipartisan caucus.

 As part of Angels in Adoption , Atlanta-based Cox Enterprises was recognized as CCAI's Corporate National Angel "for its longstanding commitment to strengthening communities, supporting families, and investing in opportunities that help people and communities thrive. Through its corporate philanthropy, employee volunteerism, and community partnerships, Cox works to address barriers and expand opportunity." The annual Angels in Adoption celebration, held at the Capitol Turnaround in Washington, drew Sens. Amy Klobuchar (D-Minn.) and Chuck Grassley (R-Iowa) and Rep. Bennie Thompson (D-Miss.).

